  "review": "docs/art/distinct-terrain-batch-04.md",
  "acceptance": "Independent code and visual re-review provisionally pass. Controller verified all14variants/66port-densitypairs/1868opaque core seam pixels and56actual-PNG patches; full-map/runtime integration, natural fringes and hamlet approaches remain open. No original rasters.",
  "path_interior": "Path-only organic interior. Let S(t)=clamp(t,0,1)^2*(3-2*clamp(t,0,1)), E=S((minimum signed polygon-edge distance-8)/8), A=2pi(x/142+y/80), B=2pi(x/142-y/80), using world x/y. Warp local route lookup by E*(0.55*sin(A),0.55*sin(B)), displacement length <=0.55*sqrt(2)*E world px. Wear=0.2*sin(5*A+2*B+0.7)*sin(3*B-A); core radius=width/2+E*(0.4*sin(A+0.4)*cos(B)+wear). For 3+-port junctions smoothly union core SDF with a central disc of radius 0.65*width at warped coordinates: h=max(1.5-abs(core-disc),0)/1.5, merged=min(core,disc)-1.5*h*h/4, core=core+E*(merged-core). Border=border*(1-0.45*E+0.25*E*sin(B+0.7)). Pocket=S((sin(2*A+0.3)*cos(3*B-0.4)+0.15)/0.9); bank opacity=1-0.75*E*pocket; final alpha=outer_AA*(core_AA+(1-core_AA)*bank_opacity). The 8-world-pixel edge zone is unchanged; full variation begins at 16 px. Cores stay opaque; irregular translucent earth verges reveal underlying terrain without baked-in grass. Road and stream arithmetic is unchanged."
}
